Actually, `memcmp` on null-terminated strings is fine since both `d_name` values are NUL-terminated and `memcmp` will stop at the first difference or at the NUL (which is 0 < any positive byte). Use this simpler version:

```c
static int dirent_name_cmp(const void *a, const void *b)
{
    const struct dirent *da = *(const struct dirent *const *)a;
    const struct dirent *db = *(const struct dirent *const *)b;
    return memcmp(da->d_name, db->d_name,
